comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T10:34:31.518Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: live focused searches, open/in-progress lists and a complete strict 3023-item all-status read found no matching open item. Read the governance parent and full pm-gh1440 metadata/comments/history: that completed work covers none/source context admission and truthful unexecuted refusals, while this report adds validation of run-only options before combined link edits. Reuse that predecessor as related context; keep this distinct report open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-20T11:29:18.698Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: admit all run directives and effective post-edit selection before link writes; preserve genuine executed failure receipts. Shared PR with runtime SDK option admission pm-fl3phm. Current corpus is complete across 3025 items, including closed lineage; no unrelated item is claimed."
  "2026-10-20T11:36:18.538Z","harness:codex","Regression proof: new owned-sandbox integration controls failed on the pre-fix head because an invalid combined test request appended tests_add history and persisted the link before refusing. Candidate first pass preserves authoritative bytes for syntax/selection refusals, validates the effective list inside the item lock, requires run for timeout/progress, and keeps actual child failures distinct. Existing 19 linked-test editing tests pass; broader verification is underway."
  "2026-10-20T11:54:21.518Z","harness:codex","Latest published pm-changelog2026.10.20 installs and passes deep package doctor. Separate existing upstream PR262 changes closed-issue classification, identifies upstream owner pmc-txk1, and is BLOCKED with unresolved local release-check timing risks in its live PR evidence. It is not consumed or merged by this implementation; current repaired issues have concrete linked source/tests and closure evidence. Retain the upstream distinction rather than treating its pending work as published behavior."
  "2026-10-20T13:17:14.654Z","harness:codex","Linked verification passed22 tests across2 real integration files, with isolated schema trackers and recorded execution evidence. First hosted head passes coverage, compatibility, Windows, packed installation and security contexts; only graph composition failed on two missing typed relationships, now corrected through CLI. Genuine child execution failures retain their prior evidence semantics."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T11:46:44.698Z","harness:codex","Validate syntax before side effects, and validate selectors against the effective post-edit list inside the item mutation lock. An execution failure after successful admission may retain accepted edits and run history; a preflight refusal must not."
